<title>SLOVAKIA: SLOVAK VSZ H1 '97 NET FALLS SHARPLY.</title>
<headline>SLOVAK VSZ H1 '97 NET FALLS SHARPLY.</headline>
<dateline>BRATISLAVA 1997-08-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results for six-month period</p>
<p>ending June 30, 1997:</p>
<p>(in million crowns)</p>
<p> After-tax profit	     398.829  vs	776.733</p>
<p> Operating revenues	28,080.694  vs   23,239.296</p>
<p> Operating costs	   29,050.193  vs   21,647.429</p>
<p> Operating result	    -969.499  vs   +1,591.867</p>
<p> Financial revenues	 2,870.853  vs	583.222</p>
<p> Financial costs	    1,365.146  vs	826.241</p>
<p>Result from financial</p>
<p>  operations		  1.505,707  vs     -243.019</p>
<p> Total loans		 13,056.440  vs   10,779.616</p>
<p> Long-term loans	    9,154.680  vs    7,868.949</p>
<p> Short-term loans	   3,901.760  vs    2,910.667</p>
<p> Reserves		     1,458.776  vs    2,712.534</p>
<p> Basic capital	     16,449.263  vs   16,449.263</p>
<p> Total assets		58,649.047  vs   58,718.923</p>
<p>Note. Full company name is VSZ a.s., the country's largest</p>
<p>integrated steel producer.</p>
<p>-- Bratislava Newsroom, 42-7-210-3687</p>
</text>
